{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. You’re here because of shortness of breath and chest tightness. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. It started a few days ago. I had trouble breathing even at rest, and a dry cough. I went to urgent care and they thought it was esophageal spasms, gave me diltiazem. I felt okay for a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, and then what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Then it came back—tightness in my chest and shortness of breath again. I tried my Flovent inhaler, but it didn’t help. I went back to the ER, and they said it might be GERD. Then yesterday, my PCP sent me here because they were worried about a clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. In the ER, they did a CT scan to check for a pulmonary embolism. Good news—it ruled that out. Your troponin was normal, so we don’t think it’s a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s a relief. But why am I still so short of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lungs have some wheezing, and you have a history of childhood asthma. We think this is reactive airway disease—like an asthma flare-up. The prednisone you started yesterday should help reduce inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Wait—I used my inhaler a few times yesterday, but it didn’t help. Was it the wrong one?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you used Flovent, which is a maintenance inhaler. It doesn’t work for sudden symptoms. You need albuterol for quick relief. We’ll make sure you have that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t know that. That makes sense. So what’s the plan now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue the prednisone for five days, give you albuterol nebulizers, and start a new inhaler called Symbicort. It combines a steroid and a long-acting bronchodilator to prevent flare-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my other medicines? I take pills for diabetes, blood pressure, and acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re continuing your blood pressure and acid reflux meds. For diabetes, we’re holding your glyburide because steroids can raise blood sugar. We’ll monitor that closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my migraines? I take Topamax and propranolol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2139-12-02 19:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep those. You also have a history of pseudotumor cerebri—we’ll watch for any headache changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2139-12-03 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2139-12-03 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better, I think. Still some cough, but the breathing feels a bit easier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2139-12-03 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. Your labs show your white count was a bit high yesterday, but it’s coming down. Likely from the steroids, not an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2139-12-03 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I was worried about that. So it’s not pneumonia?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2139-12-03 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, your chest X-ray was clear. No signs of infection. We’re on the right track with the asthma treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2139-12-03 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I fell earlier when I stood up. I got dizzy and hit my head. I didn’t pass out, but I have a small headache now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2139-12-03 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad you told me. Let’s get a CT of your head to be safe. And we’ll check your blood pressure and heart rhythm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2139-12-03 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT scan came back normal—no bleeding or injury. Your ECG was stable too. The dizziness might be from standing too fast, or possibly from the Ativan you’re taking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2139-12-03 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take lorazepam for anxiety. Could that make me unsteady?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2139-12-03 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially with other medications. We’re going to lower your dose to 0.5 mg as needed, to help prevent another fall."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2139-12-03 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Can I still go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2139-12-03 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re hoping so. Your breathing is improving. We’ll keep monitoring you, and if all goes well, you could go home in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2139-12-04 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your breathing sounds much better—no wheezing today. Your oxygen levels are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2139-12-04 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! I feel like I can take deeper breaths now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2139-12-04 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs today are also improving. We’ll get you set up with your discharge medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2139-12-04 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I still need the prednisone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2139-12-04 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, finish the full five-day course. And you’ll go home with Symbicort—two puffs twice a day—and albuterol for rescue if symptoms return."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2139-12-04 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And stop the Flovent, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2139-12-04 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Symbicort replaces it. We’ll also give you a nicotine patch—you mentioned you still smoke?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2139-12-04 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been trying to quit. This might help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2139-12-04 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can. Smoking makes asthma worse. We strongly recommend quitting for your lung health."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2139-12-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—the CT scan showed two tiny nodules in your right lung. They’re very small, only 3 mm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2139-12-04 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Are they cancer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2139-12-04 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not likely. Given your smoking history, we recommend a follow-up CT in one year to check them. Most nodules like this don’t change."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2139-12-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re clearing you to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2139-12-05 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2139-12-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your PCP as planned. Also, you’re scheduled with a pulmonologist for pulmonary function tests to better understand your asthma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2139-12-05 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my headache from the fall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2139-12-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should resolve. We gave you Ultram for a few days if needed. If it gets worse or you feel confused, go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2139-12-05 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I feel much better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2139-12-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep using your inhalers as directed, quit smoking, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2139-12-02 19:09:00",
    "admission_end": "2139-12-05 14:12:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of type 2 diabetes, hypertension, GERD, asthma, and tobacco use was admitted for shortness of breath and chest tightness. Initial evaluation ruled out pulmonary embolism and cardiac ischemia. She was diagnosed with reactive airway disease and treated with a prednisone burst, albuterol nebulizers, and initiation of Symbicort. Her symptoms improved during the hospital stay. On the second day, she had a fall with head impact; CT head was normal, and lorazepam was reduced to minimize fall risk. She was discharged home with inhaler education, smoking cessation support, and plans for pulmonary follow-up and lung nodule surveillance. Chronic conditions were managed, and glycemic control was maintained with insulin due to steroid-induced hyperglycemia.",
    "problems": [
      "Chronic obstructive asthma with (acute) exacerbation",
      "Reactive airway disease",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified",
      "Fall with head trauma",
      "Lung nodules"
    ]
  }
}
